[1] causal spectral factor of the saturated split (per frame mode, W = c|k| = 1)
    Laplace identity int_0^inf J0(Wt) e^(iwt - eta t) dt = (W^2 + (eta - i w)^2)^(-1/2): max rel. error over 12 points (eta = 0.2, 0.05) = 1.7e-15
    eta -> 0+: w= 0.50: |H|^2 = 1.333333e+00 vs 1/|W^2-w^2| = 1.333333e+00
    eta -> 0+: w= 0.99: |H|^2 = 5.025126e+01 vs 1/|W^2-w^2| = 5.025126e+01
    eta -> 0+: w= 1.01: |H|^2 = 4.975124e+01 vs 1/|W^2-w^2| = 4.975124e+01
    eta -> 0+: w= 3.00: |H|^2 = 1.250000e-01 vs 1/|W^2-w^2| = 1.250000e-01
    UHP scan (Im w in [1e-6,1e2], Re w in [-5,5]): min |H| = 9.987e-03, max |H| = 7.071e+02 (finite, nonzero: H and 1/H analytic in the UHP)
    => H is causal (theta(t) J0(Wt)); 1/H = (W^2 - (w+i0)^2)^(1/2) is analytic in the UHP with |1/H| <= |w| + W: causal by Paley-Wiener-Schwartz (a distribution of order 1)
    (J0*J0)(t= 1.0) = +0.84147098 vs sin(t) = +0.84147098  [G_R = H^2 in the time domain]
    (J0*J0)(t= 5.0) = -0.95892427 vs sin(t) = -0.95892427  [G_R = H^2 in the time domain]
    (J0*J0)(t=20.0) = +0.91294525 vs sin(t) = +0.91294525  [G_R = H^2 in the time domain]
    arcsine synthesis: int cos(w't) dmu(w') = +0.9384698072 vs J0(t) = +0.9384698072 (dmu = dw'/(pi sqrt(W^2-w'^2)) >= 0 on |w'|<W)
    arcsine synthesis: int cos(w't) dmu(w') = -0.2600519549 vs J0(t) = -0.2600519549 (dmu = dw'/(pi sqrt(W^2-w'^2)) >= 0 on |w'|<W)
    arcsine synthesis: int cos(w't) dmu(w') = -0.1698542522 vs J0(t) = -0.1698542522 (dmu = dw'/(pi sqrt(W^2-w'^2)) >= 0 on |w'|<W)
    subtraction: none

[2] near-cone suppression e(s) = eps + (1-eps) s^2/(s^2+d^2) = (s^2 + eps d^2)/(s^2 + d^2), d = sqrt(eps)
    eps=1e-02: max |e_+(w)|^2/e(s) - 1 on real w = 1.0e-14; zeros at +-Re-i*5.00e-03, poles at +-Re-i*4.99e-02 (all in the LHP: e_+ and 1/e_+ outer)
      plateau: e(s=eps) = 1.98e-02 (~2 eps), e(s=sqrt(eps)) = 0.505
    eps=1e-06: max |e_+(w)|^2/e(s) - 1 on real w = 1.7e-13; zeros at +-Re-i*5.00e-07, poles at +-Re-i*5.00e-04 (all in the LHP: e_+ and 1/e_+ outer)
      plateau: e(s=eps) = 2.00e-06 (~2 eps), e(s=sqrt(eps)) = 0.500
    R11-5 profile, eps=1e-02: Stieltjes density negative on t in [1.02e-04, 9.90e-03] (min -1.34e+05): NO positive cone-centred Lorentzian measure
    R11-5 profile, eps=1e-04: Stieltjes density negative on t in [1.02e-08, 9.99e-05] (min -1.35e+09): NO positive cone-centred Lorentzian measure
    NNLS cone-centred Lorentzian fit (200 widths 1e-7..1e2), eps=1e-02: max relative error = 0.48 (no positive measure reproduces it)
    arctan member (eps=1e-04, b=0.01): D = (1/2|u|)[1+(1/eps-1)(2/pi)atan(b/|u|)] = (1/2) int rho(t) dt/(u^2+t), rho >= 0; quadrature vs closed form max rel. error = 6.4e-04
      u=1e-05: P_J/(|u|/2) = 1.001e-04
      u=1e-03: P_J/(|u|/2) = 1.068e-04
      u=1e+00: P_J/(|u|/2) = 1.547e-02
    subtraction: none

[3] single port vs parallel bank (baseband u, single-mode QND elements chi = 1/(G/2 - i u), a_i = lam sqrt(G) chi)
    cascade of 3 elements: max ||gain|/|H_x| - 1| over u in [-5,5] = 6.7e-16 (single port: exactly saturated, S_imp S_FF = |gain|^2/4)
    parallel bank, Gamma in [1e-03, 1] (8/decade, 25 elements): causal saturating combination needs the all-pass B with group delay 1.60e+04 (units 1/band) ~ 16.0/Gamma_min
    parallel bank, Gamma in [1e-06, 1] (8/decade, 49 elements): causal saturating combination needs the all-pass B with group delay 1.60e+07 (units 1/band) ~ 16.0/Gamma_min
    parallel bank, Gamma in [1e-09, 1] (8/decade, 73 elements): causal saturating combination needs the all-pass B with group delay 1.60e+10 (units 1/band) ~ 16.0/Gamma_min
    => a parallel bank is either unsaturated (R12-7: X up to 2.47) or carries a Hubble-scale record delay when Gamma_min ~ 1/t_H; the single-port factor has neither

[4] finite start: metric-record noise per mode with the saturated split, h_noise(t) = int_{t0}^t J0(W(t-t')) xi(t') dt', S_xi = 1/2
    T=1e+02/W: Var h = 1.155374 (asymptotic (ln 8WT + gamma_E)/(2 pi) = 1.155756); Var hdot/W^2 = 0.837832; energy/mode ~ W^2(Var h + Var hdot/W^2)/2 = 0.99660
    T=1e+03/W: Var h = 1.522253 (asymptotic (ln 8WT + gamma_E)/(2 pi) = 1.522224); Var hdot/W^2 = 1.203884; energy/mode ~ W^2(Var h + Var hdot/W^2)/2 = 1.36307
    T=1e+04/W: Var h = 1.888685 (asymptotic (ln 8WT + gamma_E)/(2 pi) = 1.888691); Var hdot/W^2 = 1.570388; energy/mode ~ W^2(Var h + Var hdot/W^2)/2 = 1.72954
    T=1e+05/W: Var h = 2.255158 (asymptotic (ln 8WT + gamma_E)/(2 pi) = 2.255159); Var hdot/W^2 = 1.936850; energy/mode ~ W^2(Var h + Var hdot/W^2)/2 = 2.09600
    => finite at every finite age, growing as (1/pi) ln(W T) per mode (both quadratures); stationary limit infinite (Theorem U). subtraction: none
    record energy E(T) = 2 int_0^U du P(u) sin^2(uT/2)/u^2, near-cone baseband, P(u) = e(u) sqrt(u^2+u0^2)  (u0 = s0 regulator of R11-5)
    eps=1e+00, u0=0e+00: E(T=1e4..1e14) = 9.793, 14.4, 19, 23.61, 28.21, 32.82; dE/dlnT = 1.00e+00, 1.00e+00, 1.00e+00, 1.00e+00, 1.00e+00
    eps=1e-04, u0=0e+00: E(T=1e4..1e14) = 4.607, 4.606, 4.607, 4.607, 4.608, 4.608; dE/dlnT = -1.40e-04, 1.00e-04, 1.00e-04, 1.00e-04, 1.00e-04
    eps=1e-04, u0=1e-10: E(T=1e4..1e14) = 4.607, 4.606, 4.607, 4.607, 4.623, 6.178; dE/dlnT = -1.40e-04, 1.00e-04, 1.12e-04, 3.38e-03, 3.38e-01
    => s0 = 0 (finite start, no coherence-time regulator): secular slope -> eps forever (eps ln T); s0 > 0: linear once T >> 1/s0 (referee's point)

[5] matter side at finite age (W = 1)
    null transfer (W_m = W): P(T=50) = 398.102;  P/T^2 = 0.1592  | off-cone W_m = 0.3 W: P/T = 0.5700 (stationary rate S_x(0.3) = 0.5495)
    null transfer (W_m = W): P(T=200) = 6366.300;  P/T^2 = 0.1592  | off-cone W_m = 0.3 W: P/T = 0.5553 (stationary rate S_x(0.3) = 0.5495)
    null transfer (W_m = W): P(T=800) = 101857.766;  P/T^2 = 0.1592  | off-cone W_m = 0.3 W: P/T = 0.5513 (stationary rate S_x(0.3) = 0.5495)
    => near-null decoherence finite at every age (grows ~T^2 instead of being infinite); off-cone transfers converge to the stationary rate
    finite-start correction to the off-cone stationary kernel at age T: relative ~ |J0 tail| ~ (2/(pi W T))^(1/2) per amplitude; for the rate, the
      lab k = 1/(1 um): W = 3.00e+14 s^-1, 1/(W t_H) = 7.7e-33  (subtraction: the stationary kernel)
      k = 1/AU: W = 2.00e-03 s^-1, 1/(W t_H) = 1.1e-15  (subtraction: the stationary kernel)
      k = 1/(1 kpc): W = 9.71e-12 s^-1, 1/(W t_H) = 2.4e-07  (subtraction: the stationary kernel)

